      "content": "Many economists argue that while the policy would indeed cause severe short-term disruptions to labor supply and supply chains in agriculture, hospitality, and construction, calling it a \"fundamentally destroy\" government is an overstatement based on current data. The primary risks identified in studies are immediate cost inflation and temporary shifts in wage levels, rather than a complete collapse of the economy. Ultimately, the true economic impact depends heavily on whether new immigration policies are implemented to fill the void and how the public reacts through voting and political pressure in the near future.",
